<h4 id=3D"minitems-and-maxitems" class=3D"is-toc-heading" tabindex=3D"-1"><=
a href=3D"https://developer.wordpress.org/rest-api/extending-the-rest-api/s=
chema/#minitems-and-maxitems">minItems and maxItems</a></h4>
<p>The <code>minItems</code> and <code>maxItems</code> keywords can be used=
 to constrain the acceptable number of items included in the array.</p>
<p>For instance, given the following schema, <code>[ "a" ]</code> and <code=
>[ "a", "b" ]</code> are valid, while <code>[]</code> and <code>[ "a", "b",=
 "c" ]</code> are invalid.</p>
<pre class=3D"language-php" tabindex=3D"0"><code class=3D"language-php"><sp=
an class=3D"token php language-php"><span class=3D"token keyword">array</sp=
an><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'type'</span>     <sp=
an class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token string sing=
le-quoted-string">'array'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'minItems'</span> <sp=
an class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token number">1</=
span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'maxItems'</span> <sp=
an class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token number">2</=
span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'items'</span>    <sp=
an class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token keyword">ar=
ray</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
        <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'type'</span> <sp=
an class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token string sing=
le-quoted-string">'string'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span><span class=3D"token punctuat=
ion">,</span>
<span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span><span class=3D"token punctuation"=
>;</span>
</span></code></pre>
<p>The <code>exclusiveMinimum</code> and <code>exclusiveMaximum</code> keyw=
ords do not apply, they are only valid for the <code>number</code> and <cod=
e>integer</code> types.</p>
<h4 id=3D"uniqueitems" class=3D"is-toc-heading" tabindex=3D"-1"><a href=3D"=
https://developer.wordpress.org/rest-api/extending-the-rest-api/schema/#uni=
queitems">uniqueItems</a></h4>
<p>The <code>uniqueItems</code> keyword can be used to require that all ite=
ms in the array are unique.</p>
<p>For instance, given the following schema, <code>[ "a", "b" ]</code> is v=
alid, while <code>[ "a", "a" ]</code> is not.</p>
<pre class=3D"language-php" tabindex=3D"0"><code class=3D"language-php"><sp=
an class=3D"token php language-php"><span class=3D"token keyword">array</sp=
an><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'type'</span>        =
<span class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token string s=
ingle-quoted-string">'array'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</spa=
n>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'uniqueItems'</span> =
<span class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token constant=
 boolean">true</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'items'</span>       =
<span class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token keyword"=
>array</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
        <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'type'</span> <sp=
an class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token string sing=
le-quoted-string">'string'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span><span class=3D"token punctuat=
ion">,</span>
<span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span><span class=3D"token punctuation"=
