<h5 id=3D"uniqueness" class=3D"is-toc-heading" tabindex=3D"-1"><a href=3D"h=
ttps://developer.wordpress.org/rest-api/extending-the-rest-api/schema/#uniq=
ueness">Uniqueness</a></h5>
<p>Items of different types are considered unique, for instance, <code>"1"<=
/code>, <code>1</code> and <code>1.0</code> are different values.</p>
<p>When arrays are compared, the order of items matters. So the given array=
 is considered to have all unique items.</p>
<pre class=3D"language-json" tabindex=3D"0"><code class=3D"language-json"><=
span class=3D"token punctuation">[</span>
  <span class=3D"token punctuation">[</span> <span class=3D"token string">"=
a"</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span> <span class=3D"token st=
ring">"b"</span> <span class=3D"token punctuation">]</span><span class=3D"t=
oken punctuation">,</span>
  <span class=3D"token punctuation">[</span> <span class=3D"token string">"=
b"</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span> <span class=3D"token st=
ring">"a"</span> <span class=3D"token punctuation">]</span>
<span class=3D"token punctuation">]</span>
</code></pre>
<p>When objects are compared, the order the members appear in does not matt=
er. So the given array is considered to have duplicate items since the valu=
es are the same, they just appear in a different order.</p>
<pre class=3D"language-json" tabindex=3D"0"><code class=3D"language-json"><=
span class=3D"token punctuation">[</span>
  <span class=3D"token punctuation">{</span>=20
    <span class=3D"token property">"a"</span><span class=3D"token operator"=
>:</span> <span class=3D"token number">1</span><span class=3D"token punctua=
tion">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token property">"b"</span><span class=3D"token operator"=
>:</span> <span class=3D"token number">2</span>
  <span class=3D"token punctuation">}</span><span class=3D"token punctuatio=
n">,</span>
  <span class=3D"token punctuation">{</span>
    <span class=3D"token property">"b"</span><span class=3D"token operator"=
>:</span> <span class=3D"token number">2</span><span class=3D"token punctua=
tion">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token property">"a"</span><span class=3D"token operator"=
>:</span> <span class=3D"token number">1</span>
  <span class=3D"token punctuation">}</span>
<span class=3D"token punctuation">]</span>
</code></pre>
<p>Uniqueness is checked in both <code>rest_validate_value_from_schema</cod=
e> and <code>rest_sanitize_value_from_schema</code>. This is to prevent ins=
tances where items would be considered unique before sanitization is applie=
d, but after sanitization the items would converge to identical values.</p>
<p>Take for instance the following schema:</p>
<pre class=3D"language-php" tabindex=3D"0"><code class=3D"language-php"><sp=
an class=3D"token php language-php"><span class=3D"token keyword">array</sp=
an><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'type'</span> <span c=
lass=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token string single-q=
uoted-string">'array'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'uniqueItems'</span> =
<span class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token constant=
 boolean">true</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'items'</span> <span =
class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token keyword">array=
</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
        <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'type'</span> <sp=
an class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token string sing=
le-quoted-string">'string'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
        <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'format'</span> <=
span class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token string si=
ngle-quoted-string">'uri'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</span>
    <span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span><span class=3D"token punctuat=
ion">,</span>
<span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span><span class=3D"token punctuation"=
>;</span>
</span></code></pre>
<p>A request with <code>[ "https://example.org/hello world", "https://examp=
le.org/hello%20world" ]</code> would pass validation because each string va=
lue is different. However, after <code>esc_url_raw</code> converted the spa=
ce in the first url to <code>%20</code> the values would be identical.</p>
<p>In this case <code>rest_sanitize_value_from_schema</code> would return a=
n error. As such, you should always validate and sanitize parameters.</p>
<h3 id=3D"objects" class=3D"is-toc-heading" tabindex=3D"-1"><a href=3D"http=
s://developer.wordpress.org/rest-api/extending-the-rest-api/schema/#objects=
">Objects</a></h3>
<p>Specifying a <code>type</code> of <code>object</code> requires data to b=
e an object, but that is only half the validation story. You=E2=80=99ll als=
o want to enforce the format of each object=E2=80=99s property. This is don=
e by specifying a map of property names to JSON Schemas that object members=
 must conform to using the <code>properties</code> keyword.</p>
<p>For example, the following schema requires an object where the property =
<code>name</code> is a string and <code>color</code> is a hex color.</p>
<pre class=3D"language-php" tabindex=3D"0"><code class=3D"language-php"><sp=
an class=3D"token php language-php"><span class=3D"token keyword">array</sp=
an><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'type'</span>       <=
span class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token string si=
ngle-quoted-string">'object'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</spa=
n>
    <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'properties'</span> <=
span class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token keyword">=
array</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
        <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'name'</span>  <s=
pan class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token keyword">a=
rray</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
            <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'type'</span>=
 <span class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token string =
single-quoted-string">'string'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,</s=
pan>
        <span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span><span class=3D"token punc=
tuation">,</span>
        <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'color'</span> <s=
pan class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token keyword">a=
rray</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">(</span>
            <span class=3D"token string single-quoted-string">'type'</span>=
   <span class=3D"token operator">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"token strin=
g single-quoted-string">'string'</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">,<=
